  "kind": "design",

  "state": "classified",

  "summary": "A current reading note distinguishes authenticated fetch-SSE explicit Last-Event-ID handling from EventSource automatic behavior. It scopes durable replay to orchestration, identifies existing binary live-surface routes/viewer, and preserves one-multiplexed-stream-per-client and saturated-pool input handling as unqualified design constraints rather than completed work. Browser/Device tranche: Full read; unchanged. Current viewer is per-visible-viewer, not the planned multiplex owner; no actual pool-starvation measurement. Current repo issue935 is the original ADR task, not archive935.",

  "limits": "No current all-surface connection census, saturated HTTP/1.1 pool, live reconnect/browser/native transport, or proxy deployment was measured. Per-visible-viewer implementation is not proof of the planned per-client multiplexing or its latency guarantee.",

